{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 source-only control proposal at 5e8d4a63284854eabd9c86bdb9e0645f22e6e727 (tree ce6a5873013b1bdbd7cf88f4ee5371aec5fb1514). No mutation, owner, parser, compiler or dependency command ran. The existing AE1 implementation note records no earlier mutant control; its native control-journal wording describes fixtures, not mutation evidence.\n\nRecommend two narrow controls in packages/scope/src/applications/archive-proof.ts, each using the whole packages/scope/test/archive-application-proof.test.ts owner and exact --expect title:\narchive install proof binds Base Rules, exact signed IDs and native retained byte limits without codec fallback\n\n1. Receiver binds a signed proof to the expected Directory full reference.\nUnique old literal (line44): same(proof.installation.directory, expected.directory)\nNew literal: true\nAt test line72, wrong keeps the Directory address but changes genesis. Line83 calls readApplicationArchiveProof(answer,{...expected,directory:wrong}) and asserts toBeNull(). The valid signed answer still satisfies native codec, signature, Rules and item checks. With this one condition bypassed, the reader returns the proof, so the direct expected failure is that toBeNull assertion receiving a proof object. This isolates full-reference binding; it does not claim the sender accepted a wrong Directory or that the adapter authorized export.\n\n2. Sender counts Rules and installation metadata together before full record reads.\nUnique old literal (line66): jobBytes \u003e PREPARATION_BOUNDS.metadata - rules[0]!.size\nNew literal: jobBytes \u003e PREPARATION_BOUNDS.metadata + rules[0]!.size\nThe existing oversizedMetadata fixture sets jobBytes to the metadata limit while Rules metadata has positive size. Correct code refuses metadata-limit before state.page/state.item. The faulty sum admits the combination, reaches the fixture's page read, and the sender's existing catch converts its labelled read trap to malformed-or-unsupported. The direct expected failure is test line65 toEqual({reason:\"metadata-limit\"}), receiving {reason:\"malformed-or-unsupported\"}. This is an assertion failure, not an uncaught trap. The later line66 zero-read assertion is not expected to run after that failure. This proves the combined pre-materialization bound, not the receiver's entire charge ledger.\n\nAfter actual-main composition and root review, run the ordinary compatibility prerequisite once, then one retained-helper invocation per fault, sequentially:\nnode scripts/cloudflare-pool-compat.mjs\nnode \"$RETAINED_CONTROL\" packages/scope/src/applications/archive-proof.ts 'same(proof.installation.directory, expected.directory)' 'true' --expect 'archive install proof binds Base Rules, exact signed IDs and native retained byte limits without codec fallback' -- packages/scope --config vitest.worker.config.ts test/archive-application-proof.test.ts\nnode \"$RETAINED_CONTROL\" packages/scope/src/applications/archive-proof.ts 'jobBytes \u003e PREPARATION_BOUNDS.metadata - rules[0]!.size' 'jobBytes \u003e PREPARATION_BOUNDS.metadata + rules[0]!.size' --expect 'archive install proof binds Base Rules, exact signed IDs and native retained byte limits without codec fallback' -- packages/scope --config vitest.worker.config.ts test/archive-application-proof.test.ts\n\nRETAINED_CONTROL denotes a fresh external copy of the maintained scripts/control.mjs with only successful scratch cleanup disabled, as previously accepted. Keep the original and exact one-line diff. Use a fresh external directory per control/TMPDIR; preserve both JSON reports, raw stdout/stderr, argv, exit and wall time. Record actual registered/pass/fail/skip/cancel counts; do not infer runtime counts from the two source test declarations. Verify exact source bytes and mode restoration and a clean head. No third green run. Stop on the first unexpected failure, unloaded test, count change or inconclusive result. Read the actual failed assertion before accepting distinction.\n\nThe unchanged strict reader and metadata fixture need correspondence checks after gs2_audit's actual-main composition; the worker config shown here includes this whole owner and excludes only other named/scale files. Neither control uses security-entry-points as a mutant witness or changes any expected hash. The whole-owner positive run also exercises genuine v1/v2 signed packets in native SQLite, but Rules/job fold metadata are explicit stand-ins. Current publisher-trust revocation and genuine second-install/root authority remain separate shared-Base/shared-Grow runtime witnesses, not claims from these two controls. All commands above remain UNRUN.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:43fa0d748aea541ed335caafb06537adc6803b1b stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466"}}